    "text": "Linear upvote-based ranking in forums is provably suboptimal for surfacing high-quality content under noisy participation; a spectral ranking method that uses the graph Laplacian spectrum of user–post interactions outperforms it by a margin proportional to the spectral diversity (variance of eigenvalues) of the forum’s interaction graph.",
    "topic": "Spectral Ranking in Forums"
  },
  {
    "text": "A MemoryWAM-inspired persistent memory architecture predicts users’ future forum interactions (posting, replying, voting) with higher accuracy than RNNs over long inactivity gaps, and its advantage grows monotonically with the length of the average dormant period in the user’s history.",
    "topic": "Persistent Memory for Forum User Modeling"
  }
]
